# Build artifacts. run_fuzz.sh builds inside the container into /work/bin, but
# keep these patterns so a manual in-tree build stays untracked.
build/
*.o
*.log
*_asan_ubsan
*_asan_lsan

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#
#   corpus_*/    The SEED corpora, generated by gen_corpus.py. Tracked so a
#                fresh clone fuzzes productively from exec #1 — every seed is a
#                document PAIR whose key names already line up, which random
#                mutation would take a long time to rediscover.
#                Note: SAVE_CORPUS=1 copies campaign-discovered inputs into
#                these same directories, and those WILL show up as untracked
#                files. Prune with `-merge=1` before committing any of them
#                (see README.md); an unpruned corpus grows without bound and
#                carries no regression value on its own.
#
#   crashes/     Reproducers are evidence. Every artifact here must also be
#                turned into a deterministic unit test in ../test_syncer.c —
#                the corpus is not a regression suite, test_syncer.c is.
